# {{NAME}} wiki RAG

Optional local retrieval over `{{WIKI}}/**/*.md`, generated by the `wiki-rag` skill.
The Markdown wiki stays canonical; everything here is derived and rebuildable.

```bash
cd tools/{{NAME}}-rag && npm ci --no-audit --no-fund && cd ../..
node tools/{{NAME}}-rag/rag.mjs models     # downloads ~2.3 GB of GGUF models (explicit, network)
node tools/{{NAME}}-rag/rag.mjs prepare    # index + embeddings into .{{NAME}}-rag/
node tools/{{NAME}}-rag/rag.mjs status     # read-only probe
node tools/{{NAME}}-rag/rag.mjs search "exact words"   # BM25
node tools/{{NAME}}-rag/rag.mjs vector "a question"     # embeddings, seconds
node tools/{{NAME}}-rag/rag.mjs query  "a question"     # hybrid + reranker; minutes on CPU
node --test tests/{{NAME}}-rag.Tests.mjs
```

`rag.config.json` holds the only settings: `name`, `wiki` (relative to the project root) and
`device` (`auto` = Metal, CUDA, Vulkan or CPU as available; `cpu` = force CPU).
Editing the wiki makes the index stale until the next `prepare`; queries then refuse and
report `semantic-index-stale` instead of serving old chunks.

| Model | Size | Used by |
|---|---|---|
| embeddinggemma-300M Q8_0 | ~0.33 GB | `vector`, `query`, `prepare` |
| Qwen3-Reranker-0.6B Q8_0 | ~0.64 GB | `query` |
| qmd-query-expansion-1.7B q4_k_m | ~1.28 GB | `query` |
